1️⃣ Frontend Config (React/Vue SPA)
# /etc/nginx/sites-available/frontend.conf


File path of the Nginx config. Not executed; just reference.

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name example.com www.example.com;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}


listen 80; → Nginx listens for HTTP requests.

server_name ... → Domains this server responds to.

return 301 https://$host$request_uri; → Redirect all HTTP requests to HTTPS permanently.

server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    server_name example.com www.example.com;


listen 443 ssl http2; → Listen for HTTPS traffic and enable HTTP/2 for faster connections.

server_name → Domains for HTTPS server.

    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/example.com/privkey.pem;


Specifies SSL certificate and key for HTTPS.

    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    ssl_ciphers 'ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256';
    ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;
    ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;


ssl_protocols → Only allow secure TLS versions.

ssl_ciphers → Only allow strong encryption.

ssl_prefer_server_ciphers → Server chooses ciphers, not client.

ssl_session_cache → Cache SSL sessions for performance.

    access_log /var/log/nginx/frontend_access.log;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/frontend_error.log;


Access and error logs for monitoring and debugging.

    root /var/www/frontend/build;
    index index.html;


root → Path to static frontend files.

index → Default file if URL is a folder.

    location / {
        try_files $uri /index.html;  # SPA routing
    }


Serve requested file if it exists; otherwise, serve index.html for SPA routing (React/Vue).

    location /static/ {
        alias /var/www/frontend/build/static/;
        access_log off;
        expires 30d;
    }


Serve static assets from /static/.

alias → Map URL to folder.

access_log off; → Don’t log static file requests.

expires 30d; → Cache browser files for 30 days.

    add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "no-referrer-when-downgrade" always;
    add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload" always;


Security headers explained line by line (clickjacking, MIME sniffing, XSS protection, referrer policy, HTTPS enforcement).
Let’s break them line by line:

1️⃣ add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;

Purpose: Prevents your website from being embedded in <iframe>s on other domains.

Why: Stops clickjacking attacks.

SAMEORIGIN → Only allow embedding your own pages, not from other sites.

always → Ensures header is sent even on errors.

2️⃣ add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;

Purpose: Stops browsers from trying to “guess” the content type of a file.

Why: Prevents MIME-type sniffing attacks (e.g., executing malicious scripts).

nosniff → Tells browser to trust the declared Content-Type header.

3️⃣ add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;

Purpose: Enables the browser’s built-in XSS (cross-site scripting) filter.

1 → Enable XSS filter.

mode=block → If an attack is detected, block rendering the page.

Note: Modern browsers have mostly deprecated this because they rely on Content-Security-Policy instead, but it’s still harmless to include.

4️⃣ add_header Referrer-Policy "no-referrer-when-downgrade" always;

Purpose: Controls what referrer information (the previous page URL) is sent when users click links.

no-referrer-when-downgrade → Send the referrer only when navigating from HTTPS → HTTPS. Don’t send it when going from HTTPS → HTTP.

Why: Protects privacy and avoids leaking sensitive URLs.

5️⃣ add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload" always;

Purpose: Enforces HTTPS.

max-age=31536000 → Browsers will remember to use HTTPS for 1 year.

includeSubDomains → Applies HTTPS enforcement to all subdomains.

preload → Allows your domain to be added to browser preload lists (HTTPS-only by default).
